	abstract = {Conversational agents are gaining popularity with the increasing ubiquity of smart devices. However, training agents in a data driven man- ner is challenging due to a lack of suitable corpora. This paper presents a novel method for gathering topical, unstructured conversa- tional data in an efficient way: self-dialogues through crowd-sourcing. Alongside this pa- per, we include a corpus of 3.6 million words across 23 topics. We argue the utility of the corpus by comparing self-dialogues with stan- dard two-party conversations as well as data from other corpora.
},
	bdsk-file-1 = {}}

