  keywords     = {film analysis},
  abstract     = {{Contemporary popular culture is awash with
                  particular forms of interpretation, such as
                  \enquote{drilling down} into subtexts, and the
                  explication of mysterious narrative worlds in film
                  and TV. Vulgarized approaches they may be, but they
                  allow a path into the history of forms of film
                  analysis performed by critics and scholars, forms
                  defined, variously, as close or distant, deep or
                  superficial, interpretive or descriptive. This essay
                  traces the influence of New Criticism, structuralism
                  and poststructuralism, digital data mining and other
                  trends upon the various movements and schools of
                  film analysis, and also considers the changing
